fans of american pickers were shocked  when frank fritz suddenly departed the  show in 2021 did he really leave on bad  terms and what was his life like before  the hit series keep watching to find out  although antiquing may seem like a hobby  for older people looking to reminisce  about the past a passion for collecting  can develop at any age for renowned  picker frank fritz the desire to start  collecting began as a kid he told  sidewalks entertainment  you know i collected all the staples  when i was a kid and it just escalated  he recalled collecting beer cans stamps  coins and razor blades and his passion  for beer cans continued through his  career becoming one of his signature  finds on the show fritz continued to  collect through his adolescence moving  on to big ticket items like motorcycles  and dirt bikes started out buying dirt  bikes like it was mini bikes and i went  to bigger motorcycles although he  enjoyed the hobby he didn't pursue  antiquing as a career after graduating  from high school it wouldn't be until  about 25 years later that he'd begin his  journey into becoming a picker  although their relationship may seem  strained now the natural chemistry  between fritz and costar mike wolfe  wasn't entirely staged for the show the  dynamic duo knew each other long before  any cameras started rolling brits and  wolf met in middle school and both  graduated from high school in iowa which  is where their shared passion for  picking blossomed however fritz told the  sun that the two weren't necessarily  friends right off the bat although they  both began collecting his children it  was wolf who initially started recording  himself while antiquing and pitching the  idea for the show to different networks  according to southeastern antiquing and  collecting magazine that's a good day to  be a picker wolff had to convince fritz  to join him in his videos this meant  leaving behind fritz's brick and mortar  antique store frank's finds where he  primarily sold firehouse memorabilia and  collectibles  after fritz agreed the two would drive  around and record themselves on the way  to picking sites finally i catch a break  aside from being an antique collector  reality star and entrepreneur fritz is  also an avid vintage motorcycle fan as a  teenager one of his first antique  purchases was a 1964 harley-davidson  much to the dismay of his parents  he now owns a barn filled with vintage  motorcycles and using his knowledge of  bikes for its published how to pick  vintage motorcycles three years after  the debut of american pickers the guide  explains how to find bikes negotiate  prices and maintenance after purchase  i mean does it have a title is the frame  cracked on it what's the brakes look  like fritz is also a contributing author  on american picker's guide to picking  the sixth chapter book acts as a  companion to the television show going  into depth on specific episodes it also  offers tips and tricks for anyone  interested in getting into picking and  collecting antiques  fans didn't know what to expect  following fritz's sudden disappearance  from the show i need a break but no one  could have foreseen the controversy that  erupted between the two childhood  friends  according to entertainment weekly wolf  expressed his condolences for his  longtime friends firing in a statement  saying in part  i will miss frank just like all of you  and i pray for the very best and all  good things for him on the next part of  his journey  but his involvement in fritz's departure  didn't stop there in response to wolf's  statement fritz spoke to the sun  claiming that he'd never had a good  relationship with his co-star and adding  mike's statement was bull  somebody wrote it out for him  still it seems like the biggest issue  between the two pickers was a lack of  communicating during fritz's hiatus for  the show fritz told the sun that his  co-star never called to check in on him  following a major back surgery which  left him with 185 stitches and two rods  in his back he alleged he knows i hurt  my back everyone in the whole network  knew i hurt my back but did one person  just one call and see how i was no no no  no no  fritz has always been relatively private  when it comes to his personal life but  sometimes personal issues get too big to  hide before he was officially off  american pickers he took time off for a  serious back surgery and went public  with his decision to enter rehab for  alcohol abuse he entered a treatment  facility in iowa for 77 days according  to the sun he spoke about the reasoning  behind his decision saying i didn't like  drinking anymore my mom was an alcoholic  and she died five years ago and it was  alcohol related my grandfather was an  alcoholic and he died that didn't sit  well with me but that's not the first  time fritz's substance abuse was in the  news in 2017 fritz was arrested after  driving the wrong way on the iowa  interstate he was charged with an owi  and admitted to drinking and taking a  dose of xanax before getting behind the  wheel according to wqad it was fritz's  first offense  fritz has been public with his ongoing  health issues especially his battle with  crohn's disease which is a type of  inflammatory bowel disease that can  cause serious health complications  including weight loss abdominal pain  dehydration and anemia there's no cure  for it although it's often treated with  steroids or immunosuppressants in 2013  fans began to question fritz's sudden  weight loss following a brief hiatus  during seasons 8 and 9. to avoid any  rumors he spoke openly about his  diagnosis on social media saying i have  an illness called crohn's disease which  at times is difficult to deal with i  started losing weight and ran with it  fritz spoke with the sun to explain that  he had lost 65 pounds due to a change in  diet to help manage his symptoms  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

